# ${project_name}

Install Python dependencies with `uv sync`. Start Redis at the `QUEUE_URL`
configured in `.env`, then run `uv run python artisan queue:work`.

Use `--workers 4` to start four worker processes. Register tasks in
`tasks/example_task.py` and dispatch them with `await task.kiq(...)`.
Run the generated broker test with `uv run pytest`.

For a selected database, configure `.env` and run `uv run python artisan db:migrate`.
`QUEUE_DRIVER=memory` is available for tests and in-process development;
it does not transport jobs between separate worker processes.
